{"name":"Burning Gold","hex":"#ccaa77","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of burn"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["So hot as to seem to burn (something).","Feeling very hot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burning"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burning Gold (1927 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Gold is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by John W. Noble and starring Herbert Rawlinson, Shirley Palmer and Sheldon Lewis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Burning_Gold_%281927_film%29.jpg/330px-Burning_Gold_%281927_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Gold_(1927_film)"},{"title":"Burning Gold (1936 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Gold is a 1936 American drama film directed by Sam Newfield and starring William Boyd, Judith Allen and Lloyd Ingraham. It is a modern-day western about a World War I veteran who becomes a wildcat prospector for oil and enjoys a major strike."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/Burning_Gold_1936_poster.jpg/330px-Burning_Gold_1936_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Gold_(1936_film)"},{"title":"Burning Gold (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Burning Gold\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Christina Perri for her second studio album, Head or Heart (2014). The song was written by Perri and Kid Harpoon and produced by John Hill and Butch Walker. It was first released through the iTunes